    <summary>How do you price jobs?</summary>
    <p>After we diagnose the issue, we explain recommended options and pricing before work begins. You’ll know what to expect for labor, materials, and any permits required in your municipality.</p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary>Tank vs. tankless water heaters: which is better in Texas?</summary>
    <p>Both can perform well. Tank units are often lower upfront cost; tankless provides endless hot water and can save energy when sized correctly. We assess your usage, gas or electric service, and venting to recommend a fit for your home.</p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary>My drains keep backing up. Do I need a camera inspection?</summary>
    <p>Recurring stoppages can signal bellied lines, root intrusion, or partial collapse, which is common in older Houston neighborhoods. A camera inspection shows exactly what’s happening underground so we aren’t guessing.</p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary>Are you licensed and insured?</summary>
    <p>We operate with the appropriate state and local licensing for plumbing work and carry liability coverage for your protection.</p>
  </details>
  <details>
    <summary>Will you protect my floors and walls?</summary>
    <p>Our crews use drop cloths and shoe covers and clean the work area when finished. If drywall or tile access is required for a repair, we discuss the approach beforehand.</p>
  </details>
